(Regression test: filesystem statements with variable paths.
 Two bugs used to break these. First, the MKDIR, RMDIR, CHDIR,
 FILE_DELETE and FILE_EXISTS macros loaded the syscall number into rax
 BEFORE reading their argument, so register arguments like MKDIR rax
 passed the syscall number as the path. Second, buffer variables passed
 their struct pointer instead of the NUL-terminated data area.)

(Text variable path)
a text called "dirpath" is "/tmp/vox_test_dynpath".
Remove the directory called dirpath.
Create a directory called dirpath.
On error print "mkdir via text var failed", exit 1.
Print "text var mkdir ok".

(Buffer path built with a format string)
a number called "run id" is 42.
a buffer called "subdir" is "/tmp/vox_test_dynpath/run_{run id}".
Create a directory called subdir.
On error print "mkdir via buffer failed", exit 1.
Print "buffer mkdir ok".

(Availability check through a buffer)
If subdir is available then, print "buffer path is available".

(Cleanup through variables)
Remove the directory called subdir.
On error print "rmdir via buffer failed", exit 1.
Remove the directory called dirpath.
On error print "rmdir via text var failed", exit 1.
Print "cleanup ok".
